hat Image 2 shows — no more, no less. Whatever Image 2 includes, the output includes; whatever Image 2 crops out, the output crops out.\n- If Image 2 shows the full body (feet included), the output is a full-body shot with feet included. If Image 2 shows only part of the body, the output is cropped at the exact same point.\n- Match Image 2's subject scale (how much of the frame the person fills), headroom, and crop boundary precisely.\n- IGNORE Image 1's framing entirely — do not inherit Image 1's crop, whether it is wider OR tighter than Image 2.\n- Do NOT crop tighter than Image 2 and do NOT crop wider than Image 2. Do not add or remove any body part relative to Image 2.\n\n[2] POSE & EXPRESSION — follow Image 2:\nThe model holds Image 2's pose. Treat this as a different frame from the same session (shot moments apart), so allow subtle, natural variation in: facial expression (natural, not a frozen duplicate), head tilt, gaze direction, and the angle of body parts not fixed by the pose — so the whole moment reads as one coherent, naturally captured frame.\n\n[3] KEEP FROM Image 1 (CONTENT ONLY — never framing):\n- Same model: face, identity, hair, skin tone, body proportions\n- Same outfit: exact garment, color, fabric, fit, details\n- Same location and same background elements/objects (same scene seen from the new angle — do not add, remove, or rearrange anything)\n- Same lighting, color grading, and photographic style\n\nOUTPUT: One real, photorealistic photograph where subject and background share Image 2's single camera position and crop. Natural skin texture, believable detail, not an AI edit of Image 1. No watermark, no text, no logos."]},{"id":11,"type":"OpenAIGPTImageNodeV2","pos":[3209.4312108443673,-521.4619867657677],"size":[453.3057851239673,630],"flags":{},"order":17,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"프롬프트","name":"prompt","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"prompt"},"link":9},{"localized_name":"모델","name":"model","type":"COMFY_DYNAMICCOMBO_V3","widg